[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Event Objects
PREFIX: ZEP-SRS-38-

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: software_requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-38-1
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Event Objects
TITLE: Static event object definition
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to define and initialize an event object at
compile time.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to signal multiple threads simultaneously using a bitmask
of independent event flags without requiring one synchronization object per flag.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-30

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-38-2
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Event Objects
TITLE: Dynamic event object initialization
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to initialize an event object at run time.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-30

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-38-3
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Event Objects
TITLE: Posting events
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to set a set of event bits in an event object
by ORing the specified bits into the current event bitmask, waking threads waiting for
any of those bits.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-30

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-38-4
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Event Objects
TITLE: Setting events
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to replace the entire event bitmask of an
event object with a new value, waking threads whose wait conditions are satisfied by
the new value.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-30

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-38-5
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Event Objects
TITLE: Masked event update
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to update a subset of event bits in an event
object, preserving bits not covered by a provided mask.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-30

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-38-6
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Event Objects
TITLE: Clearing events
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to atomically clear a specified set of event
bits in an event object.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-30

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-38-7
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Event Objects
TITLE: Wait for any event bit
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to block the calling thread until at least
one of a specified set of event bits is set in an event object, or until a timeout
expires.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want my thread to sleep until any one of a group of asynchronous
conditions has been signalled.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-30

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-38-8
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Event Objects
TITLE: Wait for all event bits
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to block the calling thread until all of a
specified set of event bits are simultaneously set in an event object, or until a timeout
expires.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-30

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-38-9
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Event Objects
TITLE: Event timeout behaviour
STATEMENT: >>>
When an event wait operation times out before the requested condition is met, the
Zephyr RTOS shall return a zero value to indicate that no matching events were received.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-30

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-38-10
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Event Objects
TITLE: Non-blocking event test
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to test whether any of a specified set of
event bits is currently set in an event object without blocking.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-30

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-38-11
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Event Objects
TITLE: Automatic event bit clearing on receipt
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall support optionally clearing the received event bits in an event
object when a thread successfully obtains them, so that each event is consumed by
exactly one waiter.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-30
